    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe app serves `POST /api/owners` (and `PUT`) through OfficeFloor function pipelines, with the request/response DTOs generated from `openapi.yml`. I added a structured address form that coexists with the flat `address`.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added `addressLine1` (optional) and `addressLine2` (optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list, so an owner supplying only structured fields is contract-valid while earlier flat-address owners still validate (backward-compatible).\n\n**Persistence**\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` columns to `Owner` (`model/Owner.java`) with getters/setters, and `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four schema dialects (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). MapStruct maps the new fields by name in both directions automatically.\n\n**Normalization + composition (`OwnerAddress.java`)**\n- `applyStructured(request)` normalizes whichever address fields are present. Structured is preferred: when `addressLine1` is non-blank after normalization, the flat `address` is composed as the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space + normalized `addressLine2` appended when `addressLine2` is present. Otherwise it falls back to the normalized flat `address`. Normalized structured values are written back onto the request so later steps persist and return them.\n\n**Validation**\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) now calls `applyStructured` then requires the composed `address` to be non-blank \u2014 i.e. an owner is valid when it has a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a flat `address`, plus `city` (and the other required fields).\n- `ValidateOwner` (PUT) applies the same composition; `ApplyOwner` carries the structured lines onto the entity.\n\nEverything that reads the owner's address (household id, postcode validation, locality) keys off `city`/`postcode` and the composed `address` stored on the entity, so all consumers see the structured values when present and the flat address otherwise.\n\n**Tests:** `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both the structured-normalize-and-compose case and the flat-address backward-compat case pass, and the full suite is `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
